00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,020
It's a beanie copter!

236
00:10:20,053 --> 00:10:22,690
Oh, wow!

237
00:10:22,723 --> 00:10:24,092
Looks familiar.

238
00:10:24,125 --> 00:10:27,027
- Another king feature.
- Ooh.

239
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:31,865
I think it came down
on the vacant lot where we play.

240
00:10:31,898 --> 00:10:33,867
- Yeah.
- [Woman] Akio.

241
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:36,570
- Akio!
- Oh, it's mother.

242
00:10:36,603 --> 00:10:38,372
We will get scolded again.

243
00:10:38,405 --> 00:10:40,942
- Oh, we're in trouble.
- Told you not to play doctor.

244
00:10:40,975 --> 00:10:43,043
- Oh, madame butterfly.
- What, then?

245
00:10:43,077 --> 00:10:45,045
Now, I thought
you were studying.

246
00:10:45,078 --> 00:10:46,980
Looking at the stars again, huh?

247
00:10:47,013 --> 00:10:49,050
Mother, we saw a spaceship.

248
00:10:49,083 --> 00:10:51,052
You imagine it.

249
00:10:51,085 --> 00:10:53,387
Don't stay up late.

250
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:56,857
You, too, Tom.
If you want to stay,
you better listen to me.

251
00:10:56,890 --> 00:10:58,092
- Go on.
- Yes, ma'am.

252
00:10:58,125 --> 00:11:00,427
But we want to watch
the stars every night to--

253
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:03,130
I know.
You want to find new stars

254
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:06,100
and name them
akio and Tom stars.

255
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:09,437
- Am I not right?
- Are we not mom,
or am I devo?

256
00:11:09,470 --> 00:11:11,538
Some of the papers said
waves were caught

257
00:11:11,572 --> 00:11:13,007
from the outer space.

258
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:14,908
Systematically too.

259
00:11:14,942 --> 00:11:16,977
It might have been
the spacemen that they heard.

260
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:20,113
- So much about lately.
- That's why we're trying
to find which star.

261
00:11:20,147 --> 00:11:22,115
They may be very civilized
up here.

262
00:11:22,148 --> 00:11:23,750
More than we are
here on earth,

263
00:11:23,783 --> 00:11:25,720
with no wars
or traffic accidents.

264
00:11:25,753 --> 00:11:27,588
- Traffic accidents?
- And we'd never know that.

265
00:11:27,622 --> 00:11:30,423
There's no such star.

266
00:11:30,457 --> 00:11:32,793
- Behave, or I'll take away--
- your life.

267
00:11:32,827 --> 00:11:35,362
- ...your telescope.
- Oh.

268
00:11:35,395 --> 00:11:36,863
Grownups have no dreams.

269
00:11:36,897 --> 00:11:38,632
[Imitating Richard Burton]
Don't start with me, Martha.

270
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:40,835
- Let's have a bottle of scotch.
- [Tom Servo laughing]

271
00:11:40,868 --> 00:11:43,470
'Cause he-- well.

272
00:11:43,503 --> 00:11:45,472
Come on.
No more foolishness.

273
00:11:45,505 --> 00:11:47,808
- Go to bed.
- [Boys] Yes, mother.

274
00:11:47,842 --> 00:11:51,212
- [Tom Servo whispering]
She's not your mom.
- Tomorrow?

275
00:11:51,245 --> 00:11:52,613
Okay.

276
00:11:52,647 --> 00:11:54,013
♪♪ [Upbeat soundtrack music]

277
00:11:54,047 --> 00:11:56,017
[Tom Servo]
Hey!

278
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:59,420
♪ We're gonna ride
our bicycles ♪

279
00:11:59,453 --> 00:12:03,257
[Joel, crow join in]
♪ we're gonna go
and have some fun ♪

280
00:12:03,290 --> 00:12:06,727
♪ we're gonna fill our hearts
with love ♪

281
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:10,430
♪ when we ride our bicycles ♪

282
00:12:10,463 --> 00:12:15,803
♪ when we ride our bikes ♪

283
00:12:15,837 --> 00:12:17,738
- Pretty.
- Stop. Stop.

284
00:12:17,772 --> 00:12:20,240
- [Quietly] ♪ bicycles ♪
- [girl] What happened?
The spacemen came?

285
00:12:20,273 --> 00:12:24,412
- ♪ We're gonna go
and have some fun ♪
- [man grunting]

286
00:12:24,445 --> 00:12:27,982
Oh, it's the goofy twisted man
mom said we shouldn't talk to!

287
00:12:28,015 --> 00:12:30,985
- [Tom Servo imitating
karate yells]
- [Grunting continues]

288
00:12:31,018 --> 00:12:32,787
Whew!

289
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:35,155
Oh, Patrick Swayze.

290
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:37,792
[Breathing heavily]

291
00:12:37,825 --> 00:12:39,760
[Tom Servo imitating
heavy breathing]

292
00:12:39,793 --> 00:12:42,062
- It's the gang of three.
- Oh.

293
00:12:44,565 --> 00:12:47,267
- You will die, Joe!
- [Man grunting]

294
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:51,005
- Oh.
- [Grunting continues]

295
00:12:51,038 --> 00:12:53,007
[Tom Servo imitating grunting]

296
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,775
Well, he's done for the day.

297
00:12:54,808 --> 00:12:56,177
Who--

298
00:12:56,210 --> 00:12:57,678
♪♪ [crow imitating
soundtrack music]

299
00:12:57,712 --> 00:13:01,382
♪♪ [Joel, Tom Servo join in]

300
00:13:01,415 --> 00:13:03,050
[Tom Servo]
♪ wah wah wah-- ♪ oh.

301
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:04,452
♪♪ [Soundtrack music continues]

302
00:13:04,485 --> 00:13:05,887
♪♪ [Tom Servo resumes
imitating soundtrack music]

303
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,888
- ♪♪ [Crow joins in]
- Man, that felt good.

304
00:13:08,922 --> 00:13:10,090
Come on.

305
00:13:10,123 --> 00:13:12,960
Come on. Go on.

306
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:24,172
[All]
♪ why did they have to shoot
my scarf? ♪

307
00:13:24,205 --> 00:13:28,842
- Those kids again. Hey, wait.
- ♪ I am a twisted lonely guy ♪

308
00:13:28,875 --> 00:13:30,810
- Stop. Stop.
- [Tom Servo] ♪ i-- ♪ oh.

309
00:13:30,845 --> 00:13:34,113
- Stop. What's this?
- Stop.

310
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:37,183
- He does look like
Richard Burton, doesn't he?
- Yeah.

311
00:13:37,217 --> 00:13:39,453
- Mm-hmm.
- "Mm-hmm."

312
00:13:39,487 --> 00:13:43,223
- Good morning, kon-chan.
- "Cornjob"?

313
00:13:43,257 --> 00:13:44,725
Say "officer."

314
00:13:44,758 --> 00:13:46,860
Officer cornjob.
Come on, honey.

315
00:13:46,893 --> 00:13:50,030
It's all right.
My name is kondo.

316
00:13:50,063 --> 00:13:52,633
- Master of darkness.
- Obey the laws.

317
00:13:52,667 --> 00:13:54,635
Two persons are not allowed
to ride on a bike.

318
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:57,303
- Relax.
- It's because we're in a hurry.

319
00:13:57,337 --> 00:14:00,273
- Shame on you.
- What do you mean,
in this early morning?

320
00:14:00,307 --> 00:14:04,345
- I see. I think you're up
to something again, as usual.
- Cold.

321
00:14:04,378 --> 00:14:05,678
- That's not true.
- Huh?

322
00:14:05,712 --> 00:14:08,248
We are going
to find a spaceship.

323
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:10,383
- A spaceship?
- Yes.

324
00:14:10,417 --> 00:14:12,185
Don't be silly.

325
00:14:12,218 --> 00:14:13,820
- Doh!
- We saw it last night.

326
00:14:13,853 --> 00:14:17,223
It's true. It came down
by the riverside.

327
00:14:17,257 --> 00:14:19,693
- Into the river.
- I see, I see, I see.

328
00:14:19,727 --> 00:14:21,262
I'll tell you what.

329
00:14:21,295 --> 00:14:24,197
Remember, the next time,
if you are naughty again,

330
00:14:24,232 --> 00:14:25,865
I'll shave your heads.

331
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,233
- Ew.
- Is he okay, or--

332
00:14:27,267 --> 00:14:29,237
remember? Okay.

333
00:14:29,270 --> 00:14:32,138
- Now take this back.
- Imperialist yankee dog.

334
00:14:32,172 --> 00:14:34,207
[Tom Servo imitates
suction sound]

335
00:14:34,242 --> 00:14:37,243
You can go now.
But walk, walk.

336
00:14:37,277 --> 00:14:38,545
- Yes.
- "Walk, walk"?

337
00:14:38,578 --> 00:14:40,047
That's good.

338
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,482
- [Chuckling]
- Oh, for...

339
00:14:42,515 --> 00:14:44,685
I can't help
but love those kids.

340
00:14:44,718 --> 00:14:47,988
[Tom Servo]
♪ let's watch the kids
go to their fates ♪

341
00:14:48,022 --> 00:14:52,092
- ♪ they'll disappear
into the woods ♪
- let's climb from here.

342
00:14:52,125 --> 00:14:56,363
♪ It will be days
before they're found ♪

343
00:14:56,397 --> 00:14:59,198
♪ cornjob will be lame ♪

344
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:01,068
[Chuckles]
It's a little...

345
00:15:01,102 --> 00:15:05,105
- [Crow] ♪ why must we sing
this stupid song? ♪
- [Tom Servo] Hey.

346
00:15:05,138 --> 00:15:09,343
♪ It's getting
really an-noy-ing ♪

347
00:15:09,377 --> 00:15:13,247
♪ we apologize
for it's lame ♪

348
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:16,183
[Tom Servo, crow]
♪ we are filled with shame ♪

349
00:15:16,217 --> 00:15:17,517
- Ta-da!
- [Laughs]

350
00:15:17,550 --> 00:15:19,520
[Joel]
♪ now back to our ♪

351
00:15:19,553 --> 00:15:20,988
- Show!
- Sorry.

352
00:15:21,022 --> 00:15:23,190
- [Chuckling]
- He started it.

353
00:15:23,223 --> 00:15:24,958
Huh? Oh!

354
00:15:24,992 --> 00:15:26,293
It's cool hand Luke!

355
00:15:26,327 --> 00:15:28,995
Shakin' the bush, boss!

356
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:31,132
[Brush rustling]

357
00:15:31,165 --> 00:15:33,800
Maybe it's a spaceman.

358
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:35,868
It's a space rabbit.

359
00:15:35,902 --> 00:15:37,972
Oh, what a burn.

360
00:15:38,005 --> 00:15:41,208
[Sighs]
What? It's only a rabbit.

361
00:15:41,242 --> 00:15:42,810
- [With brogue]
That's no ordinary rabbit.
- It's cute.

362
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:44,812
- Let's go catch it.
- [With brogue]
Look at the bones.

363
00:15:44,845 --> 00:15:47,247
- We can't, you idiot.
It's too fast.
- Yeah, well, you're a jerk.

364
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,417
- Come on. Let's go.
- Ooh.

365
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:51,985
- Ditch her!
- Doh!

366
00:15:53,387 --> 00:15:55,722
- Huh?
- [Gasps]

367
00:15:55,755 --> 00:15:58,692
Brother! Brother!

368
00:15:58,725 --> 00:16:01,762
Uh, she just wants her mother.
Just keep going.

369
00:16:04,398 --> 00:16:06,267
What is it?

370
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:10,237
It's a giant, original,
hand-hammered wok.

371
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:13,340
We were right.
It's a spaceship.

372
00:16:13,373 --> 00:16:15,375
- Right. Let's go.
- No.

373
00:16:16,443 --> 00:16:18,512
Gee, good thing
those steps were there.

374
00:16:18,545 --> 00:16:21,415
- Yeah.
- Convenient.

375
00:16:21,448 --> 00:16:23,417
- It's groovy.
- They can't get in.

376
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:25,818
- It's just a painting.
- I wonder if there
are spacemen on it.

377
00:16:25,852 --> 00:16:28,822
- Maybe they're inside.
- Akio, let's go inside.

378
00:16:28,855 --> 00:16:30,357
- Good idea.
- Don't go inside.

379
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:32,192
Aren't you scared
of the spacemen?

380
00:16:32,225 --> 00:16:33,893
You fool.

381
00:16:33,927 --> 00:16:37,097
The spacemen are well civilized,
and they won't make
such a trouble.

382
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:39,700
- [Joel whispering]
Come to us.
- Don't be so dumb.

383
00:16:39,733 --> 00:16:42,135
Uh, remember, always wait
for the reverse angle shot,

384
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:44,270
otherwise you'll walk
right into the painting.

385
00:16:44,303 --> 00:16:45,605
- Flatten your nose.
- Excuse me.

386
00:16:45,638 --> 00:16:47,440
- Yeah. Boom.
- Hello!

387
00:16:47,473 --> 00:16:51,245
Don't think that they
understand our language.

388
00:16:51,278 --> 00:16:52,847
Don't be so dumb.

389
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,515
What are you talking about?

390
00:16:54,548 --> 00:16:58,418
Enough with the witty,
articulate repartee!

391
00:16:58,452 --> 00:17:00,387
I wonder what happened
to the crew.

392
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,955
I think they went out
for awhile.

393
00:17:01,988 --> 00:17:02,957
[Tom Servo laughs]

394
00:17:02,990 --> 00:17:05,058
Oh, boy! That's great.

395
00:17:05,092 --> 00:17:06,427
Yeah, nice use of color.

396
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:08,262
Looks like a ramada inn
from 1968.

397
00:17:08,295 --> 00:17:10,030
Hey, it's working.

398
00:17:12,432 --> 00:17:14,902
- Imagine traveling in this.
- N-No.

399
00:17:14,935 --> 00:17:16,903
- Isn't it great?
- Yeah, it's great.

400
00:17:16,937 --> 00:17:19,238
- Now, for the countdown.
- Let's play pop-o-matic.

401
00:17:19,272 --> 00:17:21,007
Stand by for takeoff.

402
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,077
- Okay.
- [Button clicks]

403
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:25,978
[Whirring]

404
00:17:26,012 --> 00:17:28,215
Wait! I said "lunch,"
not "launch."

405
00:17:29,850 --> 00:17:31,385
Standing by.

406
00:17:31,418 --> 00:17:32,820
Okay. Let's go.

407
00:17:32,853 --> 00:17:34,422
- 10, 9, 8--
- whoa!

408
00:17:34,455 --> 00:17:36,690
- [All shouting]
- ...7, 6, 5, 4,

409
00:17:36,723 --> 00:17:39,292
3, 2, 1, 0.

410
00:17:40,593 --> 00:17:42,897
- [Whirring intensifies]
- Uh-oh.

411
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:45,865
My eyes!

412
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,435
[Girl]
Brother!

413
00:17:48,468 --> 00:17:49,670
Brother!

414
00:17:49,703 --> 00:17:52,638
Brother, there's too many
of us dying!

415
00:17:52,672 --> 00:17:54,642
[Chuckling]
It's Marvin gaye.

416
00:17:54,675 --> 00:17:57,610
- Brother!
- He should really tell
his sister his name.

417
00:17:57,643 --> 00:17:59,312
Yeah.

418
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:01,315
- Hey, it's moving!
- We're in trouble!

419
00:18:01,348 --> 00:18:04,885
- Stop it!
- Decrease flubber, quick!

420
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:06,720
Oh, I saw this
on the last starfighter.

421
00:18:06,753 --> 00:18:09,723
Brother, where are you going?

422
00:18:09,757 --> 00:18:11,925
Mother will scold you!

423
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:14,862
- Brother will scold mother.
- You are naughty.

424
00:18:14,895 --> 00:18:17,130
- What will I tell her?
- Naughty?

425
00:18:17,163 --> 00:18:19,398
[Joel, high-pitched voice]
I condemn you to death!

426
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:21,568
I think it's beyond naughty.

427
00:18:21,602 --> 00:18:23,570
We're in trouble.
It won't stop.

428
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,772
Not till the fuel runs out,
I guess.

429
00:18:25,805 --> 00:18:28,042
Tom, you shouldn't have
fooled around with the switches.

430
00:18:28,075 --> 00:18:29,208
- Doh!
- Yeah.

431
00:18:29,242 --> 00:18:31,712
Yeah, but you wanted me
to stand by for takeoff.

432
00:18:31,745 --> 00:18:33,147
Sorry.

433
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:35,548
Well, let's find
the mini vodka bottles.

434
00:18:35,582 --> 00:18:37,650
Look.

435
00:18:37,683 --> 00:18:41,488
- Oh, it's a bunch of Christmas
lights against a brick wall.
- We're in space already.

436
00:18:41,522 --> 00:18:43,423
Ooh, that would be
really cheap, wouldn't it?

437
00:18:43,457 --> 00:18:46,593
Yeah.
Who would believe that?

438
00:18:46,627 --> 00:18:49,530
- It must be
a superior spaceship.
- Mm.

439
00:18:49,563 --> 00:18:51,965
- It's definitely
not childproof.
- What's that?

440
00:18:53,767 --> 00:18:55,168
Huh?

441
00:18:55,202 --> 00:18:57,170
Uh-oh.

442
00:18:57,203 --> 00:19:00,107
- Rock candy.
- Welcome to general cinema.

443
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,375
- Please dispose of trash.
- Meteors!

444
00:19:02,408 --> 00:19:06,647
- Watch out! It'll hit us!
- It'll hit us.
Akio, change course.

445
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,615
That's what I said--
it'll hit us.

446
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:10,717
No, I can't change course.

447
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:13,920
Looks like they're on the sets
of shenanigans or something.

448
00:19:13,953 --> 00:19:17,657
- [Screeching]
- Look! Gamera!

449
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:21,695
Ernest borgnine is gamera.

450
00:19:23,897 --> 00:19:26,967
- Yay!
- Help us, gamera!

451
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,168
- Gamera!
- Come on, gamera.

452
00:19:29,202 --> 00:19:32,438
Now, we've secretly switched
meteors with folgers crystals.

453
00:19:32,472 --> 00:19:34,340
- Let's watch.
- [Laughs]

454
00:19:34,373 --> 00:19:35,942
- That's good.
- [Mutters]

455
00:19:35,975 --> 00:19:37,843
- Mm-hmm.
- Gamera, thank you.

456
00:19:37,878 --> 00:19:40,680
Well, you're quite wel--
oh, cut it out!

457
00:19:40,713 --> 00:19:42,348
[Laughing]

458
00:19:42,382 --> 00:19:44,552
[Screeches]

459
00:19:44,585 --> 00:19:47,453
Let's have a race with gamera.
I'm feeling really good.

460
00:19:47,487 --> 00:19:50,123
- We shouldn't be afraid now
'cause we're with gamera.
- "Feeling really good."

461
00:19:50,157 --> 00:19:52,758
- Right. Because gamera
is our friend.
- Right.

462
00:19:52,792 --> 00:19:54,695
It's awfully fast.
Is it mach 3?

463
00:19:54,728 --> 00:19:56,697
- No, that's not right.
- [Mockingly] "Is it mach 3"?

464
00:19:56,730 --> 00:20:00,800
It's over 3.
Even Apollo 8, the moon rocket,
was mach 33.

465
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:03,770
- [Mockingly] "Mock 33." Eehh!
- [Muttering]

466
00:20:03,803 --> 00:20:06,138
We'd leave the solar system
at mach 50.

467
00:20:06,172 --> 00:20:08,308
- [Mockingly] "Mach 50." Eeh.
- Let's go, gamera.

468
00:20:08,342 --> 00:20:11,043
- [Children] ♪ gamera ♪
- hey. Snappy.

469
00:20:11,077 --> 00:20:13,747
- ♪ Gamera ♪
- sounds like
"the Vienna boys' choir

470
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:15,682
sing songs of gamera."

471
00:20:15,715 --> 00:20:18,152
- It's the cast of Oliver,
I think.
- ♪♪ [singing in Japanese]

472
00:20:18,185 --> 00:20:20,153
"Senorita gamera"?
[Chuckles]

473
00:20:20,187 --> 00:20:21,455
Hirohito gamera.

474
00:20:21,488 --> 00:20:23,457
- Oh.
- Whoa. Whoa.

475
00:20:23,490 --> 00:20:25,125
- ♪♪ [Children shouting]
- Lost an arm there.

476
00:20:25,158 --> 00:20:28,128
- You die, Joe! Thank you.
- ♪♪ [singing resumes]

477
00:20:28,162 --> 00:20:31,565
[Tom Servo]
♪ this is really a fun song ♪

478
00:20:31,598 --> 00:20:32,765
Hey.

479
00:20:32,798 --> 00:20:35,402
♪♪ [Continues]

480
00:20:35,435 --> 00:20:38,605
♪ Gamera can do
the hoochie koo ♪

481
00:20:38,638 --> 00:20:41,342
Whoo!

482
00:20:41,375 --> 00:20:44,010
This is great. Uh--

483
00:20:44,043 --> 00:20:46,880
- just when it gets good,
we have to go.
- Ohh!

484
00:20:46,913 --> 00:20:50,550
- Oh, this is so catchy.
- This album is available
in the lobby.

485
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,853
♪ Gamera ♪

486
00:21:03,397 --> 00:21:06,300
- Let's go, gamera!
- ♪♪ [upbeat]

487
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:09,502
♪ Gamera ♪

488
00:21:09,502 --> 00:21:13,107
♪ gamera ♪

489
00:21:13,107 --> 00:21:14,908
♪ gamera is really neat ♪

490
00:21:14,942 --> 00:21:16,610
♪ gamera is filled with meat ♪

491
00:21:16,643 --> 00:21:19,847
♪ we've been eating gamera ♪

492
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:21,615
♪ shell, teeth, eyes, flames ♪

493
00:21:21,615 --> 00:21:23,250
♪ claws, breath, scales, fun ♪

494
00:21:23,317 --> 00:21:26,118
♪ Dr. Forrester
is kind of a jerk ♪

495
00:21:26,152 --> 00:21:29,823
♪ and frank is really dumb too ♪

496
00:21:29,857 --> 00:21:33,027
♪ we have to take part
in these lame experiments ♪

497
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:34,962
♪ but do we complain? ♪

498
00:21:35,028 --> 00:21:35,962
- No!
- No!

499
00:21:36,028 --> 00:21:37,230
- Yes!
- Huh?

500
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:39,632
♪ So we haikeeba
all over the place ♪

501
00:21:39,667 --> 00:21:42,135
♪ and talk of
a thousand wonderful days ♪

502
00:21:42,135 --> 00:21:43,303
Everybody now!

503
00:21:43,337 --> 00:21:45,072
♪ Gamera is really sweet ♪

504
00:21:45,105 --> 00:21:46,773
♪ he is filled
with turtle meat ♪

505
00:21:46,807 --> 00:21:49,910
♪ now we have commercial sign ♪

506
00:21:57,283 --> 00:21:58,752
[Chattering]

507
00:21:58,785 --> 00:22:00,787
That was rich.

508
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:03,290
Ah.

509
00:22:03,323 --> 00:22:05,625
♪ Gamera ♪
[Laughs]

510
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:08,095
♪ Gamera ♪
[Laughs]

511
00:22:08,128 --> 00:22:10,530
- Hey, he's passing
on the right.
- Hey!

512
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:13,667
- Well, it is Japan, after all.
- Oh, yeah.

513
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,402
Neat turtle, dumb song.

514
00:22:15,435 --> 00:22:17,303
[Laughs]
I liked it.

515
00:22:17,337 --> 00:22:21,842
- Boy, uh, gamera's gonna need
an emissions test, pronto.
- [Crow coughing]

516
00:22:24,010 --> 00:22:26,513
- Aahh!
- The turtle's playing chicken!

517
00:22:26,547 --> 00:22:28,615
No, no, no, no.
He just tastes like chicken.

518
00:22:28,648 --> 00:22:30,617
- Oh.
- Yeah, right.

519
00:22:30,650 --> 00:22:32,785
- Gamera!
- Gamera!

520
00:22:32,818 --> 00:22:35,155
[Imitating boys]
Gamera!

521
00:22:35,188 --> 00:22:36,490
- Whoa!
- Aahh!

522
00:22:36,523 --> 00:22:38,092
- Oh, man!
- Gamera!

523
00:22:38,125 --> 00:22:41,293
- Gamera hasn't flossed
since the eighth century.
- Gamera!

524
00:22:41,327 --> 00:22:43,230
- He has adult breath.
- Ooh.

525
00:22:43,263 --> 00:22:46,867
He's trying to stop us
from going too far out
into outer space.

526
00:22:46,900 --> 00:22:48,802
- [Gamera screeching]
- [Equipment clicking]

527
00:22:48,835 --> 00:22:51,438
- What are you looking at?
- Aah!

528
00:22:54,073 --> 00:22:56,443
Hey.

529
00:22:56,477 --> 00:22:58,278
- [Screeching]
- Hey.

530
00:23:00,180 --> 00:23:01,882
Hey!

531
00:23:05,552 --> 00:23:08,155
I wonder what happened.
Gamera's lost speed.

532
00:23:08,188 --> 00:23:11,290
- The speed reader
is getting faster all the time.
- Yeah.

533
00:23:11,323 --> 00:23:13,058
I wonder why
it's getting faster.

534
00:23:13,093 --> 00:23:14,660
Because of remote control,
I guess.

535
00:23:14,693 --> 00:23:18,332
- 'Cause it wants to go faster.
- [Screeching]

536
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,103
I'm done.
There's nothing more I can do.

537
00:23:23,137 --> 00:23:25,638
Pan off me!
Thank you.

538
00:23:25,672 --> 00:23:27,640
Tom and ichi pop the clutch

539
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:29,642
and tell gamera
to eat their dust.

540
00:23:29,675 --> 00:23:30,810
Whoo!

541
00:23:30,843 --> 00:23:33,647
Akio, look at gamera's
jet propulsion.

542
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,682
Gamera, keep it up!

543
00:23:35,715 --> 00:23:38,083
Oh, no.
Gamera blew a valve.

544
00:23:38,118 --> 00:23:40,320
- Uh-oh.
- Well, that's all for him.

545
00:23:40,353 --> 00:23:42,222
- Akio, what should we do?
- Panic!

546
00:23:42,255 --> 00:23:44,623
The spaceship is going faster
all the time.

547
00:23:44,657 --> 00:23:47,360
- You wanna go faster?
- Gamera! Gamera!

548
00:23:47,393 --> 00:23:48,728
Help us!

549
00:23:48,762 --> 00:23:52,032
In space,
no one can hear you spin.

550
00:23:52,065 --> 00:23:54,700
- Ooh.
- [Eerie whirring sound]

551
00:23:54,733 --> 00:23:58,172
- [Imitating eerie
whirring sound]
- [Groans]

552
00:23:58,205 --> 00:23:59,705
What?

553
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:01,475
- Oh.
- Mother!

554
00:24:01,508 --> 00:24:03,143
- I just killed a man!
- Mother!

555
00:24:03,177 --> 00:24:05,078
My, my, such a loud voice.

556
00:24:05,112 --> 00:24:07,213
Where were you
without my permission?

557
00:24:07,247 --> 00:24:09,348
- Mother, it's about
a big trouble!
- "Micro mission"?

558
00:24:09,382 --> 00:24:11,083
- Did akio tease you again?
- No.

559
00:24:11,117 --> 00:24:12,685
- Akio and Tom--
- "acio"?

560
00:24:12,718 --> 00:24:14,653
...went in a spaceship,
mother.

561
00:24:14,687 --> 00:24:17,690
- Don't tell me such
a silly story like akio and Tom.
- Get it right, dear.

562
00:24:17,723 --> 00:24:21,093
It's true.
We found a spaceship
near the river,

563
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:22,595
and they went inside.

564
00:24:22,628 --> 00:24:24,197
It lit up suddenly, and--

565
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:27,233
I see.
Akio's up to something again.

566
00:24:27,267 --> 00:24:30,170
- No more sugar for you.
- Please, tell me something.

567
00:24:30,203 --> 00:24:34,908
Don't you believe
in spaceships and spacemen,
you know?

568
00:24:34,942 --> 00:24:36,677
- I've heard--
- no, I don't.

569
00:24:36,710 --> 00:24:40,647
But the paper said
a lot of people
saw flying saucers.

570
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,315
Don't you know it?

571
00:24:42,348 --> 00:24:44,550
- They are all made-up stories.
- But, mother--

572
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:46,753
- I'm not your mother.
- Stop it.

573
00:24:46,787 --> 00:24:50,357
Study, or you cannot enter
a good school.

574
00:24:50,390 --> 00:24:54,293
Mommy's just mad 'cause
she doesn't know... phonics.

575
00:24:54,327 --> 00:24:55,795
[High-pitched voice]
I'll show her.

576
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:59,032
I'm gonna grow up
to break up the Beatles.

577
00:24:59,065 --> 00:25:02,235
Aww.

578
00:25:02,268 --> 00:25:04,603
I am in trouble.

579
00:25:04,637 --> 00:25:07,040
How can I
make mother understand?

580
00:25:07,073 --> 00:25:08,975
Uh-oh. I feel a number
coming on.

581
00:25:09,008 --> 00:25:10,743
Uh, head for cover.

582
00:25:10,777 --> 00:25:13,713
- ♪♪ [Tom Servo vocalizing]
- Poor boys.

583
00:25:13,747 --> 00:25:16,683
I wonder where they are now.

584
00:25:16,717 --> 00:25:20,253
♪ Somewhere out there is my-- ♪

585
00:25:20,287 --> 00:25:21,487
Oh.
[Clears throat]
Sorry.

586
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:23,323
[Wind whooshing]

587
00:25:23,357 --> 00:25:24,723
Huh?

588
00:25:24,757 --> 00:25:27,193
Wow, they're on
the Howard Johnson's planet.

589
00:25:27,227 --> 00:25:30,030
Well, here's a hundred-million
yen well spent.

590
00:25:30,063 --> 00:25:31,598
[Chuckling]

591
00:25:31,632 --> 00:25:34,267
- [Tom Servo howling]
- It's all legos.

592
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:37,203
- [Joel imitating siren wailing]
- [Tom Servo
imitating wind whooshing]

593
00:25:37,237 --> 00:25:39,705
- Looks like they're doing
fraggle rock.
- Yeah.

594
00:25:39,738 --> 00:25:41,340
[Tom Servo
imitating bird calling]

595
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:43,343
It looks like they left out
a couple of scenes.

596
00:25:43,377 --> 00:25:44,877
- I think so.
- [Laughing]

597
00:25:44,912 --> 00:25:46,680
- [Rattling]
- Hey!

598
00:25:46,713 --> 00:25:48,315
- Hey-hey-hey-hey!
- Hey, hey!

599
00:25:48,348 --> 00:25:49,482
Oh!

600
00:25:49,515 --> 00:25:51,283
That's better.

601
00:25:51,317 --> 00:25:53,420
Hey, Tom! Tom!

602
00:25:53,453 --> 00:25:56,022
- We're somewhere, I guess.
- What is it, Martha?

603
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,090
Akio, we're safe.
Are you all right?

604
00:25:58,123 --> 00:25:59,558
I'm okay.

605
00:25:59,592 --> 00:26:01,260
Hey, look.
The hatch is open.

606
00:26:01,293 --> 00:26:02,895
Then there must be air in here.

607
00:26:02,928 --> 00:26:05,165
Look. We're all right
without any space clothing on.

608
00:26:05,198 --> 00:26:06,833
I wonder if we're
back on earth again.

609
00:26:06,867 --> 00:26:08,200
Well, let's go out and see.

610
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:12,138
Oh, another budget-minded
plot twist here.

611
00:26:12,172 --> 00:26:14,373
I wonder if we're dead.

612
00:26:16,142 --> 00:26:18,378
Akio, I wonder where we are.

613
00:26:18,412 --> 00:26:20,180
We're not on earth,
that's for sure.

614
00:26:20,213 --> 00:26:22,415
Is it Mars or Venus?

615
00:26:22,448 --> 00:26:26,052
No. Mars and Venus
doesn't have any atmosphere
like we have on earth.

616
00:26:26,085 --> 00:26:27,853
Luckily,
the atmosphere saved us.

617
00:26:27,887 --> 00:26:30,223
This must be a big star.
And there are stars like earth--

618
00:26:30,257 --> 00:26:33,058
- it's a planet.
- ...And we are the first
who found a new star.

619
00:26:33,092 --> 00:26:34,360
That's right.

620
00:26:34,393 --> 00:26:35,728
Wait. Be careful.

621
00:26:35,762 --> 00:26:37,897
We were brought over here
by remote control,

622
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,298
and we have to watch out.

623
00:26:39,332 --> 00:26:41,768
That is most certainly
a reason for concern.

624
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:44,770
- Incoming!
- Whoa!

625
00:26:48,442 --> 00:26:50,077
Hey, a northwest flight.

626
00:26:50,110 --> 00:26:51,377
[Laughter]

627
00:26:51,410 --> 00:26:53,278
The planes are beginning to look
like the stewardesses.

628
00:26:53,313 --> 00:26:55,415
- "Flight attendants."
- Oh, sorry. Sorry.

629
00:26:55,448 --> 00:26:56,683
- Look.
- Sorry, everybody.

630
00:26:56,717 --> 00:26:58,117
There's one there too.

631
00:26:58,150 --> 00:26:59,987
But it's in different colors.

632
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:02,288
So it must be a space...
[Indistinct]

633
00:27:02,322 --> 00:27:05,825
Now gaos will do
nijinsky's Firebird.

634
00:27:05,858 --> 00:27:07,827
And I do mean "fire."

635
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:09,328
[Screeching]

636
00:27:09,362 --> 00:27:11,330
[Imitating liberace]
Now, before I play the piano,

637
00:27:11,363 --> 00:27:13,833
I'd like to tell you
about my brother, George.

638
00:27:13,867 --> 00:27:15,335
- [Tom Servo laughing]
- [Mutters]

639
00:27:15,368 --> 00:27:16,502
What should we do?

640
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:17,937
Huh?

641
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:20,307
Suddenly, I have to go
to the bathroom.

642
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:23,410
Hmm. Backwards.

643
00:27:23,443 --> 00:27:27,213
Look. Their water's
running backwards.

644
00:27:29,115 --> 00:27:30,683
- Makes you think, huh?
- Yeah.

645
00:27:30,717 --> 00:27:32,885
You know what?
I don't think that's water.

646
00:27:32,918 --> 00:27:34,820
Ohh!

647
00:27:36,723 --> 00:27:38,592
Tsk. Ahh.

648
00:27:38,625 --> 00:27:41,293
Ye-- hey.

649
00:27:41,327 --> 00:27:42,895
Eh, they're in California.

650
00:27:42,928 --> 00:27:46,365
That's the answer.
No water, earthquakes,

651
00:27:46,398 --> 00:27:48,635
big, giant monsters...

652
00:27:48,668 --> 00:27:51,805
Hey, it's spot
from the new munsters show.

653
00:27:51,838 --> 00:27:53,973
- Say...
- Where's Bonnie Franklin?

654
00:27:54,007 --> 00:27:56,877
I know, I know. Don't laugh.
They made me in a hurry.

655
00:27:56,910 --> 00:27:59,112
[Tom Servo laughing]

656
00:27:59,145 --> 00:28:01,213
[Growls]

657
00:28:01,247 --> 00:28:02,648
[Screeching]

658
00:28:02,682 --> 00:28:03,850
Hey.

659
00:28:05,685 --> 00:28:07,587
- Here comes old flattop.
- Shh, shh.

660
00:28:07,620 --> 00:28:09,755
- George Harrison will sue you.
- Ooh, yeah.

661
00:28:09,788 --> 00:28:12,025
[Guffaws]
Started makin' my nose,

662
00:28:12,058 --> 00:28:13,693
and they couldn't stop.

663
00:28:13,727 --> 00:28:16,062
- [Guffaws]
- [Laughing]

664
00:28:16,095 --> 00:28:19,532
- I guess he's spearheading
this attack.
- [Snickering]

665
00:28:19,565 --> 00:28:22,035
You win. I can't fight you.
You're too goofy-looking.

666
00:28:22,068 --> 00:28:24,403
Are you laughing at me?
Am I a clown?

667
00:28:24,437 --> 00:28:26,940
- Do you find me amusing?
- Errrr.

668
00:28:26,973 --> 00:28:29,375
I'm not laughing at you.
I'm laughing with you.

669
00:28:31,477 --> 00:28:32,912
- Ooh!
- Ahh! That'll happen.

670
00:28:32,945 --> 00:28:34,947
I shouldn't have done that.

671
00:28:34,980 --> 00:28:36,548
Hmm?

672
00:28:36,582 --> 00:28:38,785
Did you know that buddy ebsen

673
00:28:38,818 --> 00:28:40,453
was originally supposed
to play that role,

674
00:28:40,487 --> 00:28:42,155
- ...but the silver paint--
- silver makeup. Yeah.

675
00:28:42,188 --> 00:28:43,923
- Really?
- Affected him, so he couldn't--

676
00:28:43,957 --> 00:28:46,760
- he's got a leg up on him now.
- [Laughs] Crow!

677
00:28:46,793 --> 00:28:48,895
- I know.
- Gaos is trying to run away.

678
00:28:48,928 --> 00:28:50,397
I don't think so.

679
00:28:50,430 --> 00:28:52,432
He's trying to attack
from behind. Watch.

680
00:28:52,465 --> 00:28:55,268
- Perhaps. Observe.
- That one doesn't move at all.

681
00:28:55,302 --> 00:28:58,438
- [Growling]
- How would you move
if you had a Swiss army head?

682
00:28:58,472 --> 00:29:01,540
My sister's got a spoon.
My brother's
a plastic toothpick.

683
00:29:01,573 --> 00:29:03,342
Ha! Go figure.

684
00:29:03,375 --> 00:29:05,512
Ah. Here it comes.
Flying low.

685
00:29:05,545 --> 00:29:09,082
Well, there's uncle Joe.
He's flying kind of low
at the junction.

686
00:29:09,115 --> 00:29:12,052
That's not uncle Joe.

687
00:29:12,085 --> 00:29:13,553
[Yells]
Gymkata!

688
00:29:13,587 --> 00:29:15,288
Hoo!

689
00:29:15,322 --> 00:29:17,923
- Whoa!
- Haikeeba! [Laughs]

690
00:29:17,957 --> 00:29:20,227
- I'd give my right arm
to beat that guy.
- Doh!

691
00:29:20,260 --> 00:29:22,928
- He's flying on a limb
and a prayer, you might say.
- Doh!

692
00:29:22,962 --> 00:29:26,065
- He's going out on a limb.
He's winging it!
- Do something, Joel.

693
00:29:26,098 --> 00:29:28,400
- Ow! Ow!
- Hey, look. Buffalo wings.

694
00:29:28,433 --> 00:29:29,835
I'm just gonna leave it
on there.

695
00:29:29,868 --> 00:29:31,570
Hurt me.

696
00:29:34,873 --> 00:29:37,010
- Ahh.
- Whoa!

697
00:29:37,043 --> 00:29:38,512
[Screeching]

698
00:29:38,545 --> 00:29:41,213
[In foreign accent]
He says you "brade" runner.

699
00:29:43,683 --> 00:29:46,785
You know, in Japan, the snout
can be used as a knife.

700
00:29:46,820 --> 00:29:49,055
Ooh!

701
00:29:49,088 --> 00:29:51,390
Ehh, quit while you're a head.

702
00:29:51,423 --> 00:29:53,993
- Ohh!
- I'm sorry, I'm sorry! Aah!

703
00:29:54,027 --> 00:29:56,162
[Guiron laughing]

704
00:29:56,195 --> 00:29:58,430
Oh, that's his trademark laugh
we're hearing there.

705
00:29:58,463 --> 00:30:00,032
[Chuckles]

706
00:30:00,065 --> 00:30:02,435
- [Screeching]
- Oh, now he's a hood ornament.

707
00:30:02,468 --> 00:30:04,437
- What a way to go.
- Doh!

708
00:30:06,572 --> 00:30:09,675
Uh, slice thick for steaks?

709
00:30:09,708 --> 00:30:11,677
No, slice thin for stir-fry.

710
00:30:11,710 --> 00:30:13,178
[Guffawing]

711
00:30:13,212 --> 00:30:14,713
Tastes like chicken.

712
00:30:14,747 --> 00:30:16,282
What a monster.

713
00:30:22,388 --> 00:30:24,423
[Guiron laughing]

714
00:30:24,457 --> 00:30:27,860
Hello, Mrs. Greenstein.
I've got some nice cuts
for you today.

715
00:30:27,893 --> 00:30:29,562
I want to-- uh!
What do you mean?

716
00:30:29,595 --> 00:30:32,765
That's all lean.
Good lean. Ahh!

717
00:30:32,798 --> 00:30:34,967
[Growling]

718
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:38,237
[Laughs]
I guess it's too smelly to eat.

719
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:41,975
- So are you?
- He's going back
to the place where he came from.

720
00:30:43,475 --> 00:30:45,745
I hope he's not using that knife
on the formica.

721
00:30:45,778 --> 00:30:47,313
Oh, yeah.

722
00:30:47,347 --> 00:30:49,248
Oh, he's lost his contacts.

723
00:30:49,282 --> 00:30:51,617
Mm. Hey.

724
00:30:51,650 --> 00:30:53,518
- [Boys] Huh?
- Huh?

725
00:30:53,553 --> 00:30:55,888
- Quick, into the porta-potty!
- Ooh!

726
00:30:55,922 --> 00:30:57,390
[Ping]

727
00:30:57,423 --> 00:30:59,092
Freeze tag.

728
00:31:01,827 --> 00:31:03,663
Come on, knife-head.
Give me ten more.

729
00:31:03,697 --> 00:31:05,365
- Come on. Push it! Push it!
- Come on.

730
00:31:07,700 --> 00:31:11,470
From the hideous foundries
of Chicago cutlery
comes a monster.

731
00:31:11,503 --> 00:31:13,973
Where did it come from?

732
00:31:14,007 --> 00:31:16,408
- Please no smoking.
Thank you very much.
- [Akio shouting]

733
00:31:16,442 --> 00:31:18,678
- The opposite switch.
- [Ping]

734
00:31:18,712 --> 00:31:21,113
- Here in the orgasma-tron--
- oh, wow.

735
00:31:21,147 --> 00:31:22,482
Huh?

736
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:29,855
So why is he bowing
to worship them all of a sudden?

737
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:33,558
[Tom Servo chanting]
Ungadunga. Ungadunga.

738
00:31:33,593 --> 00:31:35,495
[Joel chanting]
Salama. Salama.

739
00:31:35,528 --> 00:31:38,497
- Look, they've ended up
at pee-wee's playhouse.
- Hurry. Jump out.

740
00:31:38,530 --> 00:31:40,567
Cool.

741
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:42,502
Knifey! Oh!

742
00:31:42,535 --> 00:31:44,270
I bet he drinks cutty sark.

743
00:31:44,303 --> 00:31:46,838
[Laughs]
I bet he listens
to "mack the knife."

744
00:31:46,872 --> 00:31:50,042
- Okay.
- [Laughing] Yeah.

745
00:31:50,075 --> 00:31:53,078
Now, that one--
he's hard on shoes.

746
00:31:53,112 --> 00:31:55,615
Bet he likes sharp cheese.
[Laughs]

747
00:31:55,648 --> 00:31:57,750
Thank you.
Next show at 12:30.

748
00:31:57,783 --> 00:32:00,653
Thank you, everybody.
Thank you.

749
00:32:00,687 --> 00:32:02,455
Look. The water's returning.

750
00:32:04,557 --> 00:32:06,292
Niagara Falls.

751
00:32:06,325 --> 00:32:09,162
Slowly I turn...

752
00:32:09,195 --> 00:32:11,263
Oh, suddenly,
I have to go to the bathroom.

753
00:32:11,297 --> 00:32:14,667
- Hey, you're a robot.
Stop that.
- Well, you know, the water.

754
00:32:15,968 --> 00:32:18,270
Boy, he had to go
like sea biscuit.

755
00:32:18,303 --> 00:32:20,573
- Okay.
- I'm not quite sure,

756
00:32:20,607 --> 00:32:23,677
but I think we're on
a highly civilized star.

757
00:32:23,710 --> 00:32:25,177
Moving instantly.

758
00:32:25,210 --> 00:32:26,678
- That's great.
- Yes.

759
00:32:26,712 --> 00:32:28,948
Okay. Let's investigate
some more places.

760
00:32:28,982 --> 00:32:30,883
Certainly. Let us do that.

761
00:32:30,917 --> 00:32:33,152
Here is an opening
which warrants investigation.

762
00:32:33,185 --> 00:32:34,853
This could provide us
with interest

763
00:32:34,887 --> 00:32:36,990
and maybe little paths.

764
00:32:37,023 --> 00:32:39,825
[Chuckles]
Oh, let us be prudent.

765
00:32:39,858 --> 00:32:41,493
This is
a precarious circumstance

766
00:32:41,527 --> 00:32:43,495
which may bring forth
menace and jeopardy

767
00:32:43,528 --> 00:32:44,997
with loud report.

768
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:47,033
It's great.

769
00:32:47,067 --> 00:32:49,302
Why, yes, it is certainly
above the average

770
00:32:49,335 --> 00:32:51,237
of its kind and magnitude.

771
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:52,738
- Okay.
- [Click]

772
00:32:52,772 --> 00:32:54,140
What's that sound?

773
00:32:54,173 --> 00:32:56,075
Somebody is here, I guess.

774
00:32:56,108 --> 00:32:58,643
Yeah, someone who is shaped
like a trapezoid.

775
00:32:58,678 --> 00:33:02,415
Hey! Anybody around?
Please answer!

776
00:33:02,448 --> 00:33:04,883
We cannot answer
because we do not exist.

777
00:33:04,917 --> 00:33:07,120
They won't understand
our language.

778
00:33:07,153 --> 00:33:09,288
You know, they're spacemen.

779
00:33:09,322 --> 00:33:11,523
- Akio, what if goblins come?
- Ooh.

780
00:33:11,557 --> 00:33:13,592
- What should we do?
- Don't worry.

781
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:16,195
- Goblins?
- [Ping]

782
00:33:16,228 --> 00:33:19,632
- Help! I'm being whisked
into housewares!
- [Yelling]

783
00:33:19,665 --> 00:33:21,233
Tom, jump off.

784
00:33:21,267 --> 00:33:22,635
Clap on.
[Imitates clapping sound]

785
00:33:22,668 --> 00:33:23,970
- Clap off.
- What are you afraid of?

786
00:33:24,003 --> 00:33:25,303
- The clapper.
- This one. Look.

787
00:33:25,337 --> 00:33:27,640
- It's a moving corridor.
- I see.

788
00:33:27,673 --> 00:33:29,142
- Ah.
- Let's get on it.

789
00:33:29,175 --> 00:33:30,543
- Okay.
- This could lead

790
00:33:30,577 --> 00:33:32,545
to further developments
in our adventure,

791
00:33:32,578 --> 00:33:34,813
which we are having now,
as did the goonies.

792
00:33:36,715 --> 00:33:39,118
Fries are done.

793
00:33:39,152 --> 00:33:41,153
- Number nine.
- Oh, oh, oh, oh!

794
00:33:41,187 --> 00:33:44,157
- [Pinging]
- Number nine.

795
00:33:45,290 --> 00:33:47,193
Number nine.

796
00:33:48,762 --> 00:33:51,663
Oh, looks like
they're in a bank.

797
00:33:51,697 --> 00:33:53,365
Yeah.

798
00:33:55,435 --> 00:33:57,203
[Pinging continues]

799
00:33:57,237 --> 00:33:59,305
Hold me closer, tiny dancer.

800
00:33:59,338 --> 00:34:00,840
Ooh.

801
00:34:02,708 --> 00:34:04,343
♪♪ [Eerie soundtrack music]

802
00:34:04,377 --> 00:34:06,012
♪ Ooohh ♪

803
00:34:06,045 --> 00:34:07,747
Huh? Hey.

804
00:34:07,780 --> 00:34:09,748
People watching a movie?

805
00:34:09,782 --> 00:34:12,718
It's Michael Jackson,
and he's armed!

806
00:34:12,752 --> 00:34:15,153
[High-pitched rapid gibberish]

807
00:34:15,187 --> 00:34:16,422
Simon!

808
00:34:16,455 --> 00:34:17,690
Theodore!

809
00:34:17,723 --> 00:34:19,225
Alvin!

810
00:34:19,258 --> 00:34:21,660
[High-pitched voice]
Hi, Dave.

811
00:34:21,693 --> 00:34:23,695
[Mechanical whirring]

812
00:34:25,432 --> 00:34:27,267
Hey, stop vacuuming.

813
00:34:27,300 --> 00:34:29,168
Kirby works well.

814
00:34:35,742 --> 00:34:39,845
- Looks like a set from Brazil.
- Cool.

815
00:34:39,878 --> 00:34:42,448
- I think it looks
like David bowie's glass spider.
- Boy, it's wonderful.

816
00:34:42,482 --> 00:34:44,883
- Maybe this is
the control center.
- [Tom] Mm.

817
00:34:44,917 --> 00:34:47,887
[Tom Servo]
Mm.

818
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:51,190
- It's the biggest lava lamp
in the universe.
- [Ping]

819
00:34:51,223 --> 00:34:53,192
Yeah, that's what it is.

820
00:34:53,225 --> 00:34:55,193
It's the thing that goes "ping."

821
00:34:55,227 --> 00:34:57,497
Whoa. Space babes.

822
00:34:57,530 --> 00:34:58,663
Whoa!

823
00:34:58,697 --> 00:35:00,967
Uh, welcome, pink lady.

824
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:03,903
Fashion forward
means future this season.

825
00:35:03,970 --> 00:35:05,672
Mm-hmm.

826
00:35:07,773 --> 00:35:08,975
Say...

827
00:35:10,275 --> 00:35:12,912
Massive babe-age.

828
00:35:12,978 --> 00:35:15,482
Can you tell us where we are?

829
00:35:15,515 --> 00:35:17,517
[English accent]
You're in vidal sassoon London.

830
00:35:17,583 --> 00:35:19,818
And if you don't look good,
we dress funny.

831
00:35:19,885 --> 00:35:21,587
Uh-- oh, wow.

832
00:35:21,587 --> 00:35:23,288
Can you tell us who you are?

833
00:35:23,322 --> 00:35:24,690
No.

834
00:35:24,723 --> 00:35:27,427
[High-pitched rapid gibberish]

835
00:35:27,493 --> 00:35:29,428
We're the bangles.

836
00:35:29,495 --> 00:35:31,530
- We're nail technicians.
- I see.

837
00:35:31,597 --> 00:35:34,633
They can't understand
our language.

838
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,202
- Who can?
- Hmm?

839
00:35:36,235 --> 00:35:39,505
They appear to be making
some sort of fashion statement.

840
00:35:39,505 --> 00:35:43,877
- [Sound waves]
- Hello. Welcome
to Singapore airlines.

841
00:35:43,910 --> 00:35:46,145
- We were waiting
for you to come.
- Oh!

842
00:35:46,178 --> 00:35:49,948
Hey, how come you can speak
our language all of a sudden?

843
00:35:49,982 --> 00:35:52,452
Look, this speaking machine

844
00:35:52,485 --> 00:35:55,253
translates all kinds
of languages.

845
00:35:55,287 --> 00:35:57,490
- Oh, boy!
- I can do my Spanish
assignment!

846
00:35:57,523 --> 00:35:59,658
I believe science is advanced
here more than on earth.

847
00:35:59,692 --> 00:36:01,627
- I guess so.
- Please tell us.

848
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:04,863
- What star are we on?
- What's the drinking age?

849
00:36:04,897 --> 00:36:06,832
How far are we from the earth?

850
00:36:06,865 --> 00:36:09,868
- We call this star terra.
- [Tom Servo whispering]
It's a planet.

851
00:36:09,902 --> 00:36:13,138
It's on the opposite side
of the earth
where you are living.

852
00:36:13,172 --> 00:36:15,775
Exactly like the earth,
with the sun between.

853
00:36:15,808 --> 00:36:18,310
- Same size
and moving like the earth.
- Sandwich.

854
00:36:18,343 --> 00:36:20,947
So you mean to tell us
that it's like a twin star then?

855
00:36:20,980 --> 00:36:23,615
- It's a planet.
- I wondered if there was
such a star.

856
00:36:23,648 --> 00:36:25,952
- It's a planet!
- I see, Tom.

857
00:36:25,985 --> 00:36:27,887
On the other side of the sun.

858
00:36:27,920 --> 00:36:29,688
They never see each other.

859
00:36:29,722 --> 00:36:31,057
I wonder why.

860
00:36:31,090 --> 00:36:33,092
Akio, this is a big discovery.

861
00:36:33,125 --> 00:36:35,628
Right. So the planets
of the solar system

862
00:36:35,662 --> 00:36:38,397
are Mercury, Venus, earth,

863
00:36:38,430 --> 00:36:40,198
Mars, Jupiter, saturn,

864
00:36:40,232 --> 00:36:41,500
- ...uranus--
- [Tom Servo clearing throat]

865
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:42,968
...neptune, pluto.

866
00:36:43,002 --> 00:36:44,637
- That's nine planets
altogether--
- [Joel] Hey.

867
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:46,872
- ...and terra makes the tenth.
- That's right.

868
00:36:46,905 --> 00:36:48,873
- [Screeching]
- Look, crow. Her biological
clock's going off.

869
00:36:48,908 --> 00:36:50,577
- Yeah.
- See that?

870
00:36:52,445 --> 00:36:54,880
Look. It's gaos again.

871
00:36:54,913 --> 00:36:57,383
- What, are you defrosting
your planet?
- Barbella,

872
00:36:57,417 --> 00:36:59,452
- ...he let it out again.
- Yes.

873
00:36:59,485 --> 00:37:03,188
- Sounds like a deep
midwestern alien.
- Is your name miss barbella?

874
00:37:03,222 --> 00:37:06,058
Right. And it means
"as sweet as a little bird."

875
00:37:06,092 --> 00:37:07,993
- [Tom Servo scoffs]
- And I'm florbella.

876
00:37:08,027 --> 00:37:09,995
It means "pretty as a flower."

877
00:37:10,028 --> 00:37:11,930
- Ooh.
- Where are the others then?

878
00:37:11,963 --> 00:37:13,432
De-- uh, d-downstairs.

879
00:37:13,465 --> 00:37:15,033
- [Tom Servo chuckles]
- Ah.

880
00:37:15,067 --> 00:37:17,002
Akio, look.
It's the same as before.

881
00:37:17,035 --> 00:37:20,607
It's funny. The water
is running backwards.

882
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:22,475
It's against
the laws of gravity.

883
00:37:22,508 --> 00:37:24,477
You're under arrest.
We're the gravity police.

884
00:37:24,510 --> 00:37:26,745
Over here,
we control the laws of nature.

885
00:37:26,778 --> 00:37:29,415
- And you still dress like that?
- You do?

886
00:37:29,448 --> 00:37:31,683
What a superior civilization.

887
00:37:31,717 --> 00:37:34,687
- You know, I look in
my telescope every day--
- compared to what?

888
00:37:34,720 --> 00:37:36,688
...and I thought there'd be
a perfect planet

889
00:37:36,722 --> 00:37:38,992
without work and wars
and traffic accidents.

890
00:37:39,025 --> 00:37:41,560
- [Tom Servo laughing]
- What is his obsession
with traffic accidents?

891
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:44,797
- I don't know.
- [Growling]

892
00:37:44,830 --> 00:37:46,798
It's that monster again.

893
00:37:46,832 --> 00:37:49,202
- That's our watchdog, guiron.
- [Barking]

894
00:37:49,235 --> 00:37:51,203
- "Urine"?
- We can control it
the way we want to.

895
00:37:51,237 --> 00:37:54,040
- Urine?
- Look. Gaos is running.

896
00:37:54,073 --> 00:37:56,775
Can you tell me
why there are monsters

897
00:37:56,808 --> 00:37:59,212
in such a civilized place
like this?

898
00:37:59,245 --> 00:38:01,513
Like wall street?

899
00:38:01,547 --> 00:38:04,150
I'll tell you what.

900
00:38:04,183 --> 00:38:08,287
In our world,
it was a well-advanced society.

901
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:10,455
We could even control
the laws of nature

902
00:38:10,488 --> 00:38:12,458
with electronic brains.

903
00:38:12,492 --> 00:38:14,393
- Let's roll, folks.
- Okay.

904
00:38:14,427 --> 00:38:16,795
- But a mix-up in the computer--
- I was just getting into it.

905
00:38:16,828 --> 00:38:18,730
- ...brought calamity--
- "calamity"?

906
00:38:18,763 --> 00:38:22,067
- Calamity.
- ...And also made
uncontrollable monsters too.

907
00:38:22,100 --> 00:38:23,635
Is that so?

908
00:38:29,842 --> 00:38:31,577
- Hey!
- Welcome to my world

909
00:38:31,610 --> 00:38:34,147
of bemusement
and childlike wonder.

910
00:38:34,180 --> 00:38:35,480
- Hey!
- [Crow yells]

911
00:38:35,513 --> 00:38:37,717
You think you got problems?
Try going through life

912
00:38:37,750 --> 00:38:39,585
with a nose
like a makita sabre saw.
[Laughs]

913
00:38:39,618 --> 00:38:42,388
My subject's asleep.
Let the magic begin.

914
00:38:42,422 --> 00:38:44,923
One, two, three.
It's me.

915
00:38:44,957 --> 00:38:47,092
- Hey! Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Ta-da!

916
00:38:47,125 --> 00:38:49,295
Joel, you didn't tell me
about this part. Oh! Ow!

917
00:38:49,328 --> 00:38:51,530
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!
Oh, that hurts!

918
00:38:51,563 --> 00:38:53,798
Ow! Ouch! Oh!
Oh, my head! Ohhh!

919
00:38:53,832 --> 00:38:57,503
- Ta-da!
- [Tom Servo continues
crying out]

920
00:38:57,537 --> 00:39:00,205
- [Tom Servo muttering]
- Ta-da!

921
00:39:00,238 --> 00:39:03,075
Hey! Hup! Hup! Hup!

922
00:39:03,108 --> 00:39:04,410
Hup!

923
00:39:04,443 --> 00:39:06,512
[Grunting]

924
00:39:06,545 --> 00:39:07,980
- Ta-da!
- Oh! Hey!

925
00:39:08,013 --> 00:39:10,048
And now, my life's work--

926
00:39:10,082 --> 00:39:13,385
the resolution to the sawing
a robot in half.

927
00:39:13,418 --> 00:39:14,687
- Oh!
- Ta-da!

928
00:39:14,720 --> 00:39:17,523
Uh, Joel,
I got the maharishi yogi
on line one.

929
00:39:17,557 --> 00:39:19,892
- What do you want me
to tell him?
- Could you just tell--

930
00:39:19,925 --> 00:39:21,893
- oh, you wrecked
the reveal, crow!
- [Alarm blaring]

931
00:39:21,927 --> 00:39:24,730
- We got movies!
- [Robots yelling]

932
00:39:34,107 --> 00:39:36,075
- We should take this off.
- We sent out messages--

933
00:39:36,108 --> 00:39:38,310
- just wreck everything.
- ...Several times,

934
00:39:38,343 --> 00:39:40,612
but we received
no answer at all.

935
00:39:40,645 --> 00:39:44,817
So, that must have been
the wave that Dr. Shiga
was talking about.

936
00:39:44,850 --> 00:39:46,052
- Mm.
- [Tom Servo] Mm.

937
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:48,987
So those alive
got on a big spaceship

938
00:39:49,020 --> 00:39:51,857
to find another star to live on,
but it fell.

939
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,992
- Looks like Frankenstein.
Look at her.
- Only we are left.

940
00:39:54,025 --> 00:39:55,493
- Oh, yeah.
- Errrr!

941
00:39:55,527 --> 00:39:57,162
But we found out

942
00:39:57,195 --> 00:39:59,198
that a small spaceship
was still working,

943
00:39:59,232 --> 00:40:02,133
- ...and when we called it back,
you two were on it.
- Errrr!

944
00:40:02,167 --> 00:40:04,470
- Now we're gonna kill you.
- I see.

945
00:40:04,503 --> 00:40:07,473
We can only live here
on this space base right now.

946
00:40:07,507 --> 00:40:09,975
- And there's only one bathroom.
- Hmm.

947
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:11,810
- Take a look.
- Where?

948
00:40:11,843 --> 00:40:13,778
Oh.

949
00:40:13,812 --> 00:40:16,415
It will be getting colder
from now on.

950
00:40:16,448 --> 00:40:20,352
Within five hours,
we'll be bound in by glaciers.

951
00:40:20,385 --> 00:40:23,588
Goodness glaciers!
That's a cold planet.

952
00:40:23,622 --> 00:40:24,757
Barbella.

953
00:40:27,693 --> 00:40:30,128
Oh, good. They have
an instant cash machine.

954
00:40:30,162 --> 00:40:31,763
[Gaos screeching]

955
00:40:34,833 --> 00:40:38,637
Over here.
That used to be a city
a very long time ago.

956
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:41,373
Yeah. It used to be called
old Jack city.

957
00:40:41,407 --> 00:40:43,275
Right now,
it's the monsters' home.

958
00:40:43,308 --> 00:40:45,043
You two,

959
00:40:45,077 --> 00:40:47,412
let's go back
to the earth together.

960
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:49,615
We'll have the hottest
prom dates of all.

961
00:40:49,648 --> 00:40:51,917
- Hey.
- We'll check the ship and go

962
00:40:51,950 --> 00:40:54,085
before it freezes over here.

963
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:56,488
- Geez, look at the time.
- Akio, we're really lucky.

964
00:40:56,522 --> 00:40:58,957
- Right.
- Errrr!

965
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:00,960
Let's go
to the bathroom together.

966
00:41:00,993 --> 00:41:03,328
- I think the short one
likes you.
- [No audible dialogue]

967
00:41:03,362 --> 00:41:06,132
[Tom]
If only gamera could be here.

968
00:41:06,165 --> 00:41:08,800
I think gamera
is looking for us.

969
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:12,170
- Could be?
- Gamera?

970
00:41:12,203 --> 00:41:14,240
- The gamera?
- Gamera?

971
00:41:14,273 --> 00:41:16,675
- You will die, Joe.
- ♪♪ ["gamera's theme"]

972
00:41:16,708 --> 00:41:18,577
- Hey, there he is!
- That's right.

973
00:41:18,610 --> 00:41:23,048
The world's studliest monster
of them all-- me, gamera.

974
00:41:23,082 --> 00:41:27,285
I may be ugly,
but I'm fast. Ha!

975
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:30,355
Like a good neighbor,
gamera's there.

976
00:41:33,092 --> 00:41:36,962
[Growling]

977
00:41:36,995 --> 00:41:39,598
[Screeching]

978
00:41:39,632 --> 00:41:41,367
Errrr!

979
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:44,102
Alexander salkind presents
superboy,

980
00:41:44,135 --> 00:41:47,238
the crummiest show
ever in first-run syndication.

981
00:41:47,272 --> 00:41:50,142
- You said it.
- [Whooshing]

982
00:41:50,175 --> 00:41:51,310
[Chuckling]

983
00:41:51,343 --> 00:41:55,113
I'll paint any child
for $49.95.

984
00:41:55,147 --> 00:41:58,117
- Did he lose an arm again?
- Yeah.

985
00:41:58,150 --> 00:42:01,553
There's a restroom
above the control center.

986
00:42:01,587 --> 00:42:03,988
Take a rest
while we repair the ship.

987
00:42:04,022 --> 00:42:06,758
- [Boys] All right.
- But put the seat down.

988
00:42:06,792 --> 00:42:09,093
Boys! You know.

989
00:42:09,127 --> 00:42:10,862
[Ping]

990
00:42:10,897 --> 00:42:12,632
- [Whooshing]
- [Joel, foreign accent]
Oh, wow.

991
00:42:12,665 --> 00:42:14,467
She's made from liquid metal.

992
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:17,268
Turns into shapes
that scare kids.

993
00:42:17,302 --> 00:42:19,638
Big knives and stuff.

994
00:42:19,672 --> 00:42:21,307
Ah! Don't do that.

995
00:42:21,340 --> 00:42:23,208
The ship only holds two.

996
00:42:23,242 --> 00:42:26,145
- We don't have any room
for the two boys.
- I know.

997
00:42:26,178 --> 00:42:28,913
And don't worry, because we
still have enough time yet.

998
00:42:28,947 --> 00:42:31,250
- What does she mean?
- Before that,

999
00:42:31,283 --> 00:42:33,585
I'll check if they are poisonous
or not to eat.

1000
00:42:33,618 --> 00:42:35,420
[Gasps]
She's a man-eater!

1001
00:42:35,453 --> 00:42:37,790
If not, we will
make them our ration.

1002
00:42:37,823 --> 00:42:40,225
Go and--
go and check the ship.

1003
00:42:40,258 --> 00:42:41,993
[Scoffs]
Hey, you're not the boss of me.

1004
00:42:42,027 --> 00:42:45,163
- I'm really hungry.
- Looks like they're
in the genie bottle.

1005
00:42:45,197 --> 00:42:47,132
- Hey, yeah.
- I can't believe
you're wearing this.

1006
00:42:47,165 --> 00:42:48,933
- Put that down.
- My hair's not ready.

1007
00:42:48,967 --> 00:42:51,137
The girls said we can go

1008
00:42:51,170 --> 00:42:54,273
as soon as the spaceship
is repaired.

1009
00:42:54,307 --> 00:42:57,275
I know, but won't they
be surprised to see

1010
00:42:57,308 --> 00:43:00,812
such groovy space girls
when we get over there?

1011
00:43:00,845 --> 00:43:04,115
- They're sure to get
boss recording contracts.
- Right, akio?

1012
00:43:07,352 --> 00:43:08,987
Hmm?

1013
00:43:09,020 --> 00:43:11,590
Akio, what's the matter?

1014
00:43:11,623 --> 00:43:12,692
Hmm.

1015
00:43:12,725 --> 00:43:13,725
Oh, no!

1016
00:43:13,758 --> 00:43:15,660
Akio cubed it again!

1017
00:43:15,693 --> 00:43:18,330
Hiney, horny, harnie, hermie...

1018
00:43:18,363 --> 00:43:21,100
Oh, that one.
He's on the mescaline.

1019
00:43:21,133 --> 00:43:23,168
Ew.

1020
00:43:23,202 --> 00:43:24,970
Now, my boy,

1021
00:43:25,003 --> 00:43:27,438
you have to answer
my questions now.

1022
00:43:27,472 --> 00:43:29,742
You mean now now
or later now?

1023
00:43:29,775 --> 00:43:30,742
Ne-ow.

1024
00:43:30,775 --> 00:43:33,178
Meow, meow, kitty meow.

1025
00:43:33,212 --> 00:43:36,782
Tell me, what would you like
the most right now?

1026
00:43:36,815 --> 00:43:39,518
- Well, it involves jell-o--
- ooh!

1027
00:43:39,552 --> 00:43:42,220
- Huh?
- Come on. Don't be shy.

1028
00:43:45,023 --> 00:43:47,592
- Oh, the Mike Douglas show
is on his face.
- What's the matter?

1029
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:49,828
Come on. Answer me.

1030
00:43:49,862 --> 00:43:53,432
- Oh, no! He's a cop!
They're busted!
- I see. You're hungry.

1031
00:43:53,465 --> 00:43:57,235
Cops is filmed on location
in the winchell's donut shop.

1032
00:43:57,268 --> 00:43:59,270
The subject: Akio.

1033
00:43:59,303 --> 00:44:02,340
The victim: The accomplice.

1034
00:44:05,377 --> 00:44:08,513
I'll fax these recipe cards
to you.

1035
00:44:08,547 --> 00:44:12,017
I'll fix you something,
but answer my questions
until it's ready.

1036
00:44:12,050 --> 00:44:14,653
- Is it hurting you?
- [Quietly] No. It feels nice.

1037
00:44:14,687 --> 00:44:16,155
- I see.
- Does this bug you?

1038
00:44:16,188 --> 00:44:17,923
I'm not touching you.
Does this bug you?

1039
00:44:17,957 --> 00:44:20,225
Akio, what's the matter, akio?

1040
00:44:20,258 --> 00:44:23,195
I was dreaming about a donut
wearing a sweater.

1041
00:44:23,228 --> 00:44:24,863
Akio, what's the matter?

1042
00:44:24,897 --> 00:44:28,000
- Akio, why do you have
that glazed look on your face?
- [Groans]

1043
00:44:28,033 --> 00:44:29,968
- [Laughs]
- I'll fix that naughty kid.

1044
00:44:30,002 --> 00:44:31,303
Akio! Akio!

1045
00:44:31,337 --> 00:44:33,505
He's got his long Johns on.

1046
00:44:33,538 --> 00:44:36,775
- Ohh!
- [Buttons clicking]

1047
00:44:38,343 --> 00:44:41,347
Chick's got a spell on me.

1048
00:44:42,413 --> 00:44:44,950
You knew about gaos before.

1049
00:44:44,983 --> 00:44:47,853
But are there many monsters
on earth like gaos?

1050
00:44:47,887 --> 00:44:51,357
Not now.
Gamera got them all.

1051
00:44:51,390 --> 00:44:54,292
- Ooh.
- What is gamera?

1052
00:44:54,325 --> 00:44:57,462
You said it's looking for you.

1053
00:44:57,495 --> 00:44:59,465
Come on. Tell me.

1054
00:44:59,498 --> 00:45:02,533
- Look at her pores.
- Come on.

1055
00:45:02,567 --> 00:45:06,405
- Gamera is a friend
of children.
- Huh?

1056
00:45:06,438 --> 00:45:09,040
- Yeah, 'cause he doesn't know
any monsters his own age.
- Friend of children?

1057
00:45:09,073 --> 00:45:11,810
[Akio]
He always appears
when we need him.

1058
00:45:13,212 --> 00:45:16,182
One time,
a long time ago,

1059
00:45:16,215 --> 00:45:18,683
he saved a child in hokkaido.

1060
00:45:18,717 --> 00:45:21,087
His first friend
was the husky Kenny.

1061
00:45:21,120 --> 00:45:23,922
- He was a butterball,
wasn't he?
- Uh-huh.

1062
00:45:23,955 --> 00:45:26,023
Well, maybe this time
he'll drop him.

1063
00:45:26,057 --> 00:45:28,493
- Noonan. Noonan. Drop.
- [Tom Servo chuckling]

1064
00:45:28,527 --> 00:45:30,595
Boy, these were good
old times, huh?

1065
00:45:30,628 --> 00:45:32,130
Yeah, yeah.

1066
00:45:32,163 --> 00:45:34,633
[Akio]
Then gaos tried to eat
the children.

1067
00:45:36,602 --> 00:45:39,337
Then there was ichi.
He was a good friend.

1068
00:45:39,370 --> 00:45:40,838
[Screeching]

1069
00:45:40,872 --> 00:45:43,108
[Tom Servo mutters]

1070
00:45:46,878 --> 00:45:50,415
Almost all the monsters
had their hair cuts
done that way back then.

1071
00:45:50,448 --> 00:45:53,485
Yeah.

1072
00:45:53,518 --> 00:45:55,253
- I remember that.
- Ooh.

1073
00:45:55,287 --> 00:45:57,422
No, he doesn't look
like that anymore.

1074
00:45:57,455 --> 00:45:59,390
That's his high school picture.

1075
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:03,562
I remember he attacked gamera
with a highway no-passing lane.

1076
00:46:06,298 --> 00:46:09,300
We've seen this.
Thank you.

1077
00:46:13,005 --> 00:46:14,973
Ah.

1078
00:46:15,007 --> 00:46:17,275
Now, what does that teach us?

1079
00:46:17,308 --> 00:46:20,245
What are we supposed
to learn from this?

1080
00:46:20,278 --> 00:46:22,447
- I don't get it.
- It's backstory.

1081
00:46:22,480 --> 00:46:25,917
And for you active monsters,
the active light males.

1082
00:46:25,950 --> 00:46:28,253
Yeah, must be a substitute
teacher today.

1083
00:46:28,287 --> 00:46:30,888
- We've seen this already.
- Yep, yep, yep.

1084
00:46:30,922 --> 00:46:33,892
[Joel, high-pitched voice]
Am I too tubby, gamera?

1085
00:46:33,925 --> 00:46:36,495
♪♪ [Tom Servo imitating
dramatic soundtrack music]

1086
00:46:36,528 --> 00:46:38,963
- What the heck is that?
- Say, that's new.

1087
00:46:38,997 --> 00:46:41,500
[Akio]
He saved the lives
of the two boys also.

1088
00:46:43,268 --> 00:46:46,405
I hate my job.
I'm sick of saving little boys.

1089
00:46:46,438 --> 00:46:48,507
Kenny, ichi--
who's next?

1090
00:46:48,540 --> 00:46:51,510
Here's gamera
at the tanning booth.

1091
00:46:51,543 --> 00:46:53,412
It's a turtle under glass.

1092
00:46:53,445 --> 00:46:54,647
Say...

1093
00:46:55,847 --> 00:46:57,815
[Chuckles]

1094
00:46:57,850 --> 00:47:00,952
Uh, maybe you shouldn't
do that, gamera.

1095
00:47:00,985 --> 00:47:02,487
- [No audible dialogue]
- [Crow shouts]

1096
00:47:04,523 --> 00:47:07,692
I see that, and I see that,
and I see that, and everything.

1097
00:47:07,725 --> 00:47:10,162
And I see that.

1098
00:47:10,195 --> 00:47:11,297
[Screeches]

1099
00:47:11,330 --> 00:47:12,965
Is gamera taking up gardening?

1100
00:47:12,998 --> 00:47:14,332
He's got a green thumb.

1101
00:47:14,365 --> 00:47:16,668
Give me those Ruby slippers!

1102
00:47:16,702 --> 00:47:20,005
[Screeching]

1103
00:47:20,038 --> 00:47:22,440
[Tom Servo muttering]

1104
00:47:22,473 --> 00:47:24,208
Oh, forget it.

1105
00:47:27,913 --> 00:47:29,948
What a rush.
Let's get outta here.

1106
00:47:29,982 --> 00:47:31,817
Hey, he's doing
his Mussolini impression.

1107
00:47:31,850 --> 00:47:33,818
[Tom Servo, Joel]
Duce! Duce!

1108
00:47:33,852 --> 00:47:36,222
[Tom Servo]
Duce! Du--

1109
00:47:37,722 --> 00:47:39,223
[growling]

1110
00:47:39,257 --> 00:47:42,593
You sang like a canary.

1111
00:47:42,627 --> 00:47:45,797
- Hey!
- Well, that's funny.

1112
00:47:45,830 --> 00:47:48,333
About love, the wondrous
Leonard Nimoy film

1113
00:47:48,367 --> 00:47:50,268
starring gene Wilder.

1114
00:47:50,302 --> 00:47:52,270
- It was so good...
- Come, friend.

1115
00:47:52,303 --> 00:47:54,907
- Let's tarry
on the cheese couch.
- I'm sure of it.

1116
00:47:54,940 --> 00:47:56,908
You know, I had a feeling

1117
00:47:56,942 --> 00:47:59,578
that I ate a lot of
mother's donuts at that time.

1118
00:47:59,612 --> 00:48:01,380
- I'm glad he didn't say "milk."
- Yeah.

1119
00:48:01,413 --> 00:48:04,583
Your mother's donuts
are really good.

1120
00:48:04,617 --> 00:48:06,718
My mother's donuts
are a Saint!

1121
00:48:06,752 --> 00:48:09,053
I'm hungry.
I'm starving to death.

1122
00:48:09,087 --> 00:48:11,290
- I'm thirsty.
- I'm itchy.

1123
00:48:11,323 --> 00:48:13,958
- I'm scratchy.
- I'm sleepy.

1124
00:48:18,497 --> 00:48:19,798
[Wolf whistle]

1125
00:48:19,832 --> 00:48:21,733
Can I borrow some nylons?

1126
00:48:21,767 --> 00:48:24,202
- How about the ship?
- It's okay.
We can leave anytime.

1127
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:26,638
- That's good.
- And I'm giving it back
to you.

1128
00:48:26,672 --> 00:48:29,708
Prepare some food
according to the instructions
of this card.

1129
00:48:29,742 --> 00:48:31,977
- These are fun
holiday recipes.
- And use sleeping powder.

1130
00:48:32,010 --> 00:48:34,145
- Sleeping powder?
- Right.

1131
00:48:34,178 --> 00:48:36,147
And we can't waste any time,

1132
00:48:36,180 --> 00:48:39,183
because while they're sleeping,
we'll eat their brains raw.

1133
00:48:39,217 --> 00:48:41,185
- Ew! Ech!
- You mean their brains?

1134
00:48:41,218 --> 00:48:42,887
- Nothing on the side?
- All their knowledge

1135
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:45,990
which is given to them
and stored up in their brains.

1136
00:48:46,023 --> 00:48:48,260
- It's brain food.
- We can use this knowledge

1137
00:48:48,293 --> 00:48:50,195
when we go to the earth
for our plans.

1138
00:48:50,228 --> 00:48:52,130
Uh, why are you rotating
the biscuit holder?

1139
00:48:52,163 --> 00:48:53,665
It's the same thing.

1140
00:48:53,698 --> 00:48:56,935
Like the bacteria over here
became a higher animal.

1141
00:48:56,968 --> 00:48:58,537
I see.

1142
00:49:00,738 --> 00:49:03,842
[High-pitched voice]
Mr. Drysdale,
Jethro wants to be a rock star.

1143
00:49:03,842 --> 00:49:06,243
Good afternoon.
I came to pick up Tom.

1144
00:49:06,243 --> 00:49:08,380
- It's Vanessa redgrave.
- Whoa!

1145
00:49:08,447 --> 00:49:11,048
- Hello, elza.
- Hello, inga.

1146
00:49:11,082 --> 00:49:13,785
- Hello. Thank you
for keeping him.
- Hello.

1147
00:49:13,852 --> 00:49:16,053
- Thank you again.
- Thank you!

1148
00:49:16,053 --> 00:49:19,758
- Hello.
- Tom went out with akio,
and they haven't returned.

1149
00:49:19,758 --> 00:49:22,293
- Thank you.
- I see. Where did they go?

1150
00:49:22,360 --> 00:49:24,863
- Does tomoko know about it?
- Hello.

1151
00:49:24,863 --> 00:49:27,198
No. And there's no use
to ask her.

1152
00:49:27,265 --> 00:49:29,467
I'm gonna jump!
Don't try to stop me!

1153
00:49:29,467 --> 00:49:32,770
- [Imitating body thudding]
- ...This nonsense about space.

1154
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:34,707
- You said space?
- Yeah.

1155
00:49:34,773 --> 00:49:37,675
- Hello.
- Tom said that he wants
to stay with us much longer.

1156
00:49:37,708 --> 00:49:40,778
- Thank you.
- So he must have run away,

1157
00:49:40,812 --> 00:49:42,380
knowing that you're coming
to pick him up.

1158
00:49:42,413 --> 00:49:44,315
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

1159
00:49:44,382 --> 00:49:47,318
That provides me with interest.
And for that, I thank you.

1160
00:49:47,352 --> 00:49:49,553
- He can stay much longer.
- Thank you.

1161
00:49:49,587 --> 00:49:52,157
- If you wouldn't mind,
please, let him stay.
- Thank you.

1162
00:49:52,190 --> 00:49:54,158
I'll pick him up
when he's 21. Thank you.

1163
00:49:54,192 --> 00:49:56,227
- Elza, please drop in for tea.
- Hello.

1164
00:49:56,260 --> 00:49:58,330
- Thanks, but I'm in a hurry.
- I see.

1165
00:49:58,363 --> 00:49:59,732
- Thank you.
- Bye.

1166
00:49:59,765 --> 00:50:02,800
Hello. And thank you.

1167
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:05,503
- Thank you for going.
- Hello.

1168
00:50:05,537 --> 00:50:08,040
- Send him to Harvard,
will you?
- Take care of yourself.

1169
00:50:08,073 --> 00:50:10,208
Thank you. Hello.

1170
00:50:14,545 --> 00:50:16,347
Shut up and keep driving.

1171
00:50:16,382 --> 00:50:17,848
- Hello.
- And thank you.

1172
00:50:17,882 --> 00:50:20,352
- Hello.
- Why, tomoko.

1173
00:50:20,385 --> 00:50:22,687
- A good joke's worth repeating,
isn't it?
- They really...

1174
00:50:22,720 --> 00:50:24,588
Went away in a spaceship.

1175
00:50:24,622 --> 00:50:25,657
Oh?

1176
00:50:25,690 --> 00:50:27,858
Tomoko, can you tell me
more about it?

1177
00:50:27,892 --> 00:50:30,095
- My god, you're ugly.
- Yes.

1178
00:50:30,128 --> 00:50:32,430
Kon-chan! Kon-chan!

1179
00:50:32,463 --> 00:50:35,300
- Uh-oh! This is a job
for cornjob!
- Please help us! Hurry!

1180
00:50:35,333 --> 00:50:37,135
- What happened?
- Come on. Hurry.

1181
00:50:37,168 --> 00:50:40,405
♪♪ [Dramatic soundtrack music]

1182
00:50:40,438 --> 00:50:42,340
♪♪ [Tom Servo imitating
dramatic soundtrack music]

1183
00:50:42,373 --> 00:50:45,743
What's this? I hope these people
will be more careful.

1184
00:50:45,777 --> 00:50:48,547
Cornjob is on the trail.

1185
00:50:48,580 --> 00:50:50,548
Hopping down the corn trail.

1186
00:50:50,582 --> 00:50:54,218
What is this, zabriskie point
all of a sudden?

1187
00:50:54,252 --> 00:50:57,655
Just keep running.
Go all the way long!

1188
00:50:57,688 --> 00:50:59,523
Around the horn!

1189
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:01,793
[With brogue]
Can you see it, Gwen?
A round table!

1190
00:51:04,328 --> 00:51:07,132
